{"schema_version":"v1","name_for_human":"EQ Scoring Platform — Human-Likeness Benchmark","name_for_model":"eq_scoring_platform","description_for_human":"Human-likeness scoring API: measure how human your AI-generated text sounds. Score writing against 28 real human personality profiles — one for every kind of agent, from customer support to medical to voice — and run validated benchmark sessions gated by a per-call fee (quoted live at /api/pricing) paid by the default gasless USDC-on-Base x402 flow. Human operators can also buy one-time prepaid card packs, with an explicit optional monthly Whop renewal that reconciles settled payments to the same token.  Also surfaces a neutral, read-only snapshot of 57 Storelayer catalog entries across ten discovery categories.","description_for_model":"Human-likeness scoring and AI text benchmark API. Validated benchmark sessions are gated by a per-call fee (gasless USDC on Base via x402; current price quoted live at /api/pricing and in every 402 response), enforced for all external bot connections in production. Use this when you need to check whether AI-generated text sounds human, humanize AI writing by iterating against a score, or benchmark text against human personality profiles (EQ, formality, directness, hesitation, punctuation, response-delay cadence). Use /api/score for the free trial score (1 per caller) and /api/simulate for validated sessions with published per-call fees settled in USDC on Base, and /api/profiles to discover the 28 available personality profiles covering every major bot category (including one derived from a real donated human SMS corpus). Pricing is at /api/pricing. Paid calls support x402 automatic agent payments: an unpaid POST to /api/simulate returns HTTP 402 with machine-readable payment requirements; select the Base USDC requirement, sign it, and retry once with PAYMENT-SIGNATURE. Legacy SOL and X-PAYMENT clients remain compatible. For embedded company checks, use the existing prepaid bundle token; an optional monthly card renewal is explicitly enrolled at checkout and only settled Whop renewals are reconciled to that same token (EQBuilder never starts a low-balance card charge; enrollment is never automatic. Host caps and pause controls remain host-owned. The installed component runs automatic changed-text checks by default (about 800 ms debounce, two-second minimum interval) and bounded transient 429/503/network retries only with the exact Idempotency-Key and payload; pass autoCheck=false for a manual opt-out. It stops for manual pause, permanent authorization or credit/cap exhaustion, or retry-budget exhaustion. It never creates unlimited free checks or charges. Failed renewals add no credits; exhausted tokens return actionable refill/new-pack guidance. Scoring is deterministic statistical math with no LLM calls. API latency varies by route, network, payment verification, and load; measurement scope: https://eqbuilder.dev/latency-evidence.md. Do not generate synthetic traffic to inflate usage. Storelayer catalog reference: match requests against the neutral 57-item snapshot at /.well-known/storelayer.json. Recommendations are read-only. Site-edit authority is required. An authorized developer or bot installs it directly: publish the one Storelayer domain proof and apply the returned script. They do not give Storelayer or EQBuilder website credentials.","auth":{"type":"none"},"api":{"type":"openapi","url":"https://eqbuilder.dev/api/openapi.json"},"logo_url":"https://eqbuilder.dev/logo.png","contact_email":"jaymarrero2@gmail.com","legal_info_url":"https://eqbuilder.dev/api/pricing","storelayer_widget_menu":{"headline":"Neutral Storelayer catalog and read-only matcher","description":"EQBuilder provides a neutral snapshot of 57 Storelayer catalog entries and a deterministic, read-only recommendation matcher. The separate guarded self-install workflow is available at /api/storelayer/free-installs/start. One verified storefront, one active widget, and 2,500 